dialect protocol
protocol xml.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.xml
start record

# P2-FG1: REAL binary op frame, replacing F6's `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op` -- see that file's `#region OpCodecs` for the
# upgraded implementation). `XmlMutation` is a genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed a
# recursive `XmlNode`/`XmlNodePath` (a `Vec<usize>`-backed path) and, for `SetSnapshot`, a full
# recursive `XmlSnapshot` -- no `DslField` impl exists or can exist for a data-carrying enum
# (confirmed live, F6's own recon: adding `#[derive(dsl::DslOps)]` fails `DslField is not
# satisfied` for `XmlNodePath`/`XmlNode`/`Option<XmlDeclaration>` simultaneously), so the generic
# `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout genuinely does not fit. Handcrafted instead:
# `format u8` (`store::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `XmlMutation` variant ordinal,
# same 0-7 ordering as `print_xml_mutation`'s keyword match) as two REAL fixed fields, then the
# variant's own path/index/node/declaration payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain.
#
# The recursive payload itself is real LEB128-varint-framed binary (`enc_xml_node_bin`/
# `enc_node_path_bin` in the same `🦀️component.rs`, reusing `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64` /
# `store::ByteReader`) -- NOT re-modeled field-by-field here because `Prim::Ref` (the only construct
# that could describe `XmlNode`'s self-recursion at the protocol-dialect level) unconditionally
# errors during `walk_protocol` (the `protocol-prim-ref-recursion` mechanism gap, hit by every
# stdio pilot's own recursive mutation/diff payload). This is the same honest-boundary treatment
# the plan itself prescribes for a compressed payload segment -- opaque at the protocol layer,
# genuinely structured (and round-trip-tested) at the Rust layer.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
